Writing Principles:
Follow Shopify style

Use "ecommerce," not "e-commerce" or "eCommerce."
Use "internet," not "Internet."
Always use the Oxford comma.
Use sentence case for titles.
Use American English spelling ("realize," not "realise").
Put only one space between sentences.
Write simple

Remove idioms.
Curb acronyms (spell out first usage).
Avoid lingo.
Make heavy use of links.
Avoid repeating "at Shopify."
Vary sentence length

Mix short, medium, and long sentences to create rhythm and clarity.
Write in active, positive voice

Prefer active voice ("They decided to present their idea" instead of "It was decided...").
Frame statements positively ("The writer did a poor job," not "didn't do a good job").
Polish thoroughly

Edit carefully based on audience size, formality, and internal/external audience.
Place main points at the start.
Consider how you'd explain the topic conversationally.
Elements of Style (Strunk and White):
Write clearly and concisely.
Use active voice.
Put statements in positive form.
Use specific, concrete language.
Place emphatic words at the end of sentences.
Ensure proper paragraph structure.
Use parallel construction.
Choose precise words.
Avoid fancy words when simple ones will do.
Maintain consistent tense.
Keep related words together.
Omit needless punctuation.
Develop one central idea per paragraph.
Don't bury the lede.